This repository is derived from easthambuilds' recipe
https://github.com/easthambuilds/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold (Apache-2.0).
start.sh, stop.sh, scripts/, tools/, docker/Dockerfile and the .gitignore come from it. Changed here: start.sh and
stop.sh (stop.sh's mark for ops/keep_serving.sh; start.sh's --taps and --edits),
scripts/config.sh (the engine pin), scripts/common.sh (the image hash covers docker/patches/, rank 0's TF_FILL_*
settings and taps, ENGINE_ENV for both ranks, the containers' log rotation), scripts/prepare.sh (model/chat_template.jinja put in place), scripts/local.sh.example (the TF_FILL_*
settings, ENGINE_ENV, the taps and edits) and docker/Dockerfile (docker/patches/ applied to the Zig engine). README.md is new; it reuses parts of
the recipe's README.

docker/patches/ are changes to Bertholomus AI's TensorFold fork, branch deepseek-v41-zig
(https://github.com/bertholomus/TensorFold, Apache-2.0), itself a fork of TensorFold
(https://github.com/ashhart/TensorFold, Apache-2.0). 0005-0008 are ours and not proposed upstream yet. 0009 is by
Coinupbtc, from MiaAI-Lab/DeepSeek-v4.1-Flash-1017-2x-DGX-Sparks (zig/patches/0027-tool-call-prose.patch, Apache-2.0).
0010 is bertholomus/TensorFold #36 by Blackwellboy. 0011 and 0012 are ashhart's commits 23b943cb and cf6541ad on
TensorFold's main (#1180); 0013 is ours (their test fitted to this branch).
0014-0016, 0019 and 0020 come from MiaAI-Lab/DeepSeek-v4.1-Flash-1017-2x-DGX-Sparks, zig/patches (Apache-2.0): 0010
(Mia's AI Lab's port of William J Riley's idle nap, bertholomus/TensorFold #27), 0011 (Robert Wojciechowski), 0032 (Maciej
Kowalik), 0033 (E-Zou Shen, ported here: this branch's graph key has no shard mode) and 0038 (Mia's AI Lab). 0017 and
0018 are bertholomus/TensorFold #43 by Blackwellboy (16701b4, 80fea5d). 0021, 0022 and 0024 come from the same recipe:
0049 (Lukasz Raczylo), 0035 (Hector Isaza, without the hunks that need their 0020) and 0045 (Dick Lai, ported here: this
branch has no durable tier or KV parts). 0023, 0025, 0026 and 0027 are ours. 0028 and 0029 come from the same recipe:
0064 (Hector Isaza, from 0053 of their 4-Spark recipe; without its end-to-end test file, which this branch does not
have) and 0050 (Lukasz Raczylo; three hunks applied by hand where the context differs here). Each patch carries its
author.

model/chat_template.jinja is the template the checkpoint easthambuilds/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017-EXL3-2.9bpw carries,
written by Mia's AI Lab as a port of DeepSeek's encoding/encoding.py (DeepSeek, MIT), with one change: each piece of
the prompt is written out as it is made instead of being added to one growing string.

The model weights (DeepSeek, MIT), the checkpoint, the engine, the kernel kit and NVIDIA's PyTorch container keep
their own licenses and terms; none of them is redistributed here.
